  "grids": {
    "about": "A canvas with `grid N` shows a dot every N units over the whole view, as Clarity's own diagram designer does, drawn after its drawing's `clear` (first, when it has none), in the theme's `border` color, the same size whatever the zoom. Dots closer than 8 pixels apart are thinned: every 2N, 4N, ... units, the smallest that is 8 pixels or more (`lines`: the grid, the pixels a unit takes, the units between shown dots). Code that snaps uses `snapped(value, step)`: the multiple of step nearest to value, a half rounding up; a step of 0 gives the value (`snapped`).",
